        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-mw96kqoe-lg4q4klwz6",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Set out on a two-day trip with one overnight stay in Torotoro National Park, designed for people who enjoy hiking. The park lies in the temperate dry valleys of northern Potosí, an area of deep canyons, valleys, waterfalls and caves, with traces left by large Mesozoic reptiles.\n\nTravel from Cochabamba to Torotoro by private vehicle. On arrival, check in at the El Molino hotel and have lunch. At 14:00, set out on a tour of Umajalanta Cave. Inside, narrow passages link large vaulted chambers and galleries. Stalactites and stalagmites take on unusual shapes, and an underground river forms small pools inhabited by blind fish.\n\nDinner is scheduled for 19:00. Spend the night at an expedition-style lodge. This day takes you underground in Torotoro, and the next is devoted to the canyon."
    },
